<title>UK: Clubhaus up on New Year share tip.</title>
<headline>Clubhaus up on New Year share tip.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in golf club operator Clubhaus Plc rose on Friday after the stock was included in a list of stock tips for 1997 in Investors Chronicle magazine.</p>
<p>Clubhaus shares were up 9p at 94-1/2 by 1529 GMT in volume of 277,813 shares.</p>
<p>The magazine said Clubhaus was delivering on all the promises it made when it joined the market in February and was trading on an unwarranted 20 percent discount to the market in price-earnings ratio terms.  </p>
<p>Other stocks in the magazine's list were also higher, led by Telspec Plc, which extended its early gain to be up 50p at 232-1/2 by 1533 GMT.</p>
<p>Capitol Group Plc was up 20p at 168-1/2 though no trading was recorded, Capital Industries Plc was 15p higher at 228-1/2, again on no trade, Caradon Plc was up 2p at 239-1/2 in volume of 1.4 million and Iceland Group Plc was up 3p at 88-1/2 in volume of 2.2 million.</p>
<p>Air London Plc was down 1p at 185 in volume of 1,000 shares.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
